cff-version: 1.2.0
title: ESEM sandbox
message: >-
  If you use this model or its figures, please cite it, and please say that every
  number it produces is illustrative rather than a forecast.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Mannheim
    given-names: Markus
abstract: >-
  A small agent-based model of one electricity market region, built to be read in an
  afternoon. It simulates the region hour by hour: plant is dispatched and the price
  is set by the last unit needed to meet demand. Over 20 annual steps, contracts
  move risk between the firms in it, investors decide what to build against a view
  of the future they extrapolate rather than forecast, and a procurement scheme can
  be switched on and compared against the same weather. It is a simplification of a
  larger research model, keeping that model's scarcity pricing, contract settlement
  and investment rule, and dropping everything locational. The fleet is stylised and
  the weather is synthetic.
keywords:
  - electricity market
  - reliability
  - capacity procurement
  - agent-based model
  - investment under uncertainty
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/MarkusMannheim/esem_sandbox
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-06'
